# ISRO Bharatiya Antariksh Hackathon 2026

# Infrared Image Colorization and Enhancement for Improved Object Interpretation

## Project Goal

Develop an end-to-end AI pipeline that converts low-resolution infrared (thermal) satellite images into high-resolution, realistic RGB images while preserving semantic integrity and improving downstream computer vision tasks such as object detection.

This project uses paired Landsat 8/9 satellite imagery and follows a modular architecture so that every stage can be trained, tested, and improved independently.

---

# Current Development Stage

This project is currently being developed using **20 downloaded Landsat 8/9 scenes** for demonstration and pipeline development.

The primary objective at this stage is **NOT maximum accuracy**, but to build a complete working pipeline.

After the entire system is stable, more Landsat scenes will be added and the models will be fine-tuned.

The code must therefore be written so that it automatically supports any number of dataset folders without modification.

Never hardcode dataset size.

---

# Dataset

Current Dataset

20 Landsat 8/9 scenes

Each scene contains

- Thermal Bands (.TIF)
- RGB Bands (.TIF)
- Metadata
- Angle files
- Quality bands

Future Dataset

The project should easily scale to hundreds or thousands of Landsat scenes by simply adding more folders.

---

# Input Data

GeoTIFF (.TIF)

Bands

Thermal

